WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER

The MIT terms above cover the SOURCE CODE in this repository.

They do not, and cannot, license the DATA the code collects. That data belongs
to its providers and each carries its own terms:

  SEC EDGAR       Public domain as a US government work. Free to use, subject
                  to the SEC's fair-access rules — a descriptive User-Agent
                  with a real contact address, and no more than ten requests a
                  second. Both are enforced in code.

  Yahoo Finance   Retrieved via the `yfinance` library, which is an
                  unofficial client. Yahoo's own terms restrict
                  redistribution. Price bars are therefore treated as a local
                  cache, rebuildable from source, and are not committed to
                  this repository.

  Finnhub         Free tier, subject to Finnhub's terms. News articles are
                  label infrastructure only and are likewise not committed.

Consequently `data/` is gitignored in full. The one derived artifact kept in
version control is `live-log/alerts.csv` — detector outputs computed by this
code, not redistributed vendor data.

NOT INVESTMENT ADVICE

This is a research prototype produced as an academic project. It detects a
statistical *footprint* — unusual trading before a disclosure, which has many
innocent explanations. It does not identify a person, a fund, or an intent,
and it is not evidence of wrongdoing. Nothing here is investment advice or a
recommendation to trade.
